From 93aa386605ef55ec3ccb36f2b41e18901e01f895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adorfer <adorferen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:42:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/42] qualcommax: ipq50xx: backport QPIC SPI-NAND driver

Bring the Qualcomm QPIC SPI-NAND driver (spi-qpic-snand, upstream v6.15)
and the shared qpic_common code (upstream v6.14) to the 6.6 kernel of
qualcommax, as used by OpenWrt main for ipq50xx while it was on 6.6
(8dbbca029d^: generic/backport-6.6/413-*, 415-*, 416-v6.15-*, 416-v6.16-08).

Differences to OpenWrt main:
- The patches live in qualcommax/patches-6.6 instead of generic/, so no
  other 6.6 target (ipq40xx, ipq806x, ...) is touched.
- The qcom_nandc rework (413-01, 413-02, the qcom_nandc.c parts of 413-03,
  413-04, and 414) is left out. qcom_nandc.c (raw NAND, used by ipq807x)
  stays byte-identical and keeps its private copy of the helpers;
  qpic_common.o is built only for CONFIG_SPI_QPIC_SNAND.

Sources: 4b6886d9fd, 24db75d242, 80244360ae (Christian Marangi, Robert
Marko), c5e359a236 (George Moussalem). The upstream patches keep their
original headers; adapted ones carry a [Neanderfunk: ...] note.
